course: dictionary
lesson: 3672
title: A fiver is five
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fiver is an informal word for a five-pound note in the UK. In some other countries it can mean a five-dollar note. Either way, it means five units of that country's money.
explain: Look at the words around it to work out the meaning. «At a bus stop in Glasgow a man said "Here, wee man, a fiver if you carry this bag to that car."» He offers money for carrying a bag, so a fiver must be a sum of money.
explain: In maths money problems, «a fiver» means 5. Try the swap: put "five pounds" into the sentence instead. «It costs five pounds» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Other money words can be slang too. «Quid» means a pound, and «a tenner» means ten pounds. When you are not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: A fiver is an informal word for a five-pound note in the UK.
fact: In some other countries, a fiver can mean a five-dollar note.
fact: People say «it costs a fiver» or «lend me a fiver» when they talk about money.
fact: «Quid» is slang for a pound, and «a tenner» is ten pounds.
fact: «Wee» means small in Scotland, as in «a wee man».
exercise: Mia says, «Lend me a fiver, please.» How much money does she ask for? | *Five pounds | Five pence | Ten pounds | Fifty pounds
exercise: «A fiver if you carry this bag to that car.» What does a fiver mean in this sentence? | A bag | *A five-pound note | A car | A five-minute walk
exercise: «Quid» is slang for a pound. Which word is slang for ten pounds? | Quid | Fiver | *Tenner | Wee
test: In the UK, what is a fiver? | A small bag | *A five-pound note | A bus ticket | A ten-pound note
test: A book costs a fiver and a pen costs a fiver. How much do both cost in pounds? | 20 | 15 | 5 | *10
exam: Which is the best meaning of «a fiver» in «It costs a fiver»? | Ten pounds | Five dollars in every country | *Five pounds in the UK, or five dollars in some other countries | A small bag
